openmediavault-nextcloud (8.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Bring back directory migration: the settings page can move the data
    (/var/www/html) and the MariaDB database (/var/lib/mysql) shared
    folders to other folders without shell access.
    - "Test directories" validates every folder that was changed in the
      form (not saved yet): it must exist, be writable, live on a local
      filesystem and either be empty or already hold the matching data
      (config/config.php for the data folder, ibdata1/mysql for the
      database). Free space is compared with the size of the current
      folder.
    - "Migrate data" (with a confirmation dialog) stops the stack,
      copies every changed folder with rsync (permissions, ACLs and
      xattrs preserved) and verifies each copy against its source. The
      completed migration is recorded; because the stack file mounts the
      folders through the Compose placeholder, the stack is not started
      again until the settings are saved and applied.
    - Saving is refused per changed folder until its migration has been
      recorded; afterwards the data of the folders that were actually
      changed is removed by a background task that runs right after the
      settings have been saved.
    - rsync is added to the package dependencies.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800

openmediavault-nextcloud (8.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Nextcloud file sync and share plugin for
    OpenMediaVault 8.x.
    - Settings: image tag, web port, timezone, data and database shared
      folders, database credentials, administrator credentials and the
      trusted domains.
    - The Docker Compose stack (nextcloud, db and redis) is registered
      in the openmediavault-compose plugin on save and rendered by it;
      the plugin only manages the OMV-side integration (registration,
      lifecycle, status) and never modifies Nextcloud itself.
    - Start/stop/restart/upgrade run through 'docker compose' as
      background tasks with live output.
    - Live status: container state, running Nextcloud version
      (status.php), latest upstream release and update detection, log
      viewer and rendered compose file preview.
    - Simplified and Traditional Chinese translations included.

 -- ${GITHUB_USER} <${GITHUB_USER}@users.noreply.github.com>  Wed, 08 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0800
